# i_f< chooses between two texts by a condition evaluated when the
# program runs (MC14); only the chosen one is evaluated (1 / 0 never
# is), and both have one type (here Float). Inside an expression the
# expansion is parenthesized (MC12).
== SOURCE
x := -3
"x > 0" i_f< "1; -1"
10 * "x > 0" i_f< "1; -1"
"x < 0" i_f< "0; 1 / 0"
== EXPAND
x := -3
{ @ -> (x > 0) ? 1; -1 } @
10 * ({ @ -> (x > 0) ? 1; -1 } @)
{ @ -> (x < 0) ? 0; 1 / 0 } @
== RESULT
-1
-10
0.0
